# Ties every change to an owner (.nstack/handbook/07-governance.md §7).
# Updated automatically by nstack new-module.

# approval: agent — no default owner: a path named below needs a human's approval; any other,
# a `prototype` or `standard` module's, one approval, another contributor's agent counting
# (.nstack/handbook/07-governance.md §7).

# Foundation: any change to the OS itself goes through an ADR.
/AGENTS.md                     @NapkinStack/maintainers
/.nstack/                      @NapkinStack/maintainers
/.github/                      @NapkinStack/maintainers
/.copier-answers.yml           @NapkinStack/maintainers
/.pre-commit-config.yaml       @NapkinStack/maintainers
/.yamllint.yaml                @NapkinStack/maintainers
/CONTRIBUTING.md               @NapkinStack/maintainers
/SECURITY.md                   @NapkinStack/maintainers

# The project's records: charter, cycles, rules, decisions.
/docs/                         @NapkinStack/maintainers

# Modules: a line only for one neither `prototype` nor `standard` (doctor, L6) — all are
# `standard` today.

# Contracts: the most critical boundary in the system, never orphaned (criticality high).
/contracts/                    @NapkinStack/maintainers
